 "equipment_type": "VAV terminal unit controller",
 "applies_to": "Single-duct (OPN-VAVB1-02) and fan-powered (OPN-VAVB3-02) VAV terminals controlled by the Carrier VAV Zone II.",
 "summary": "The VAV Zone II is Carrier's pressure-independent VAV box controller, sold as a single-duct model and a fan-terminal model with an integrated actuator and airflow sensor. It talks BACnet MS/TP (9600 to 76.8 kbps) or BACnet ARC156, addressed on two rotary switches, and usually exchanges data with its VAV Master and air source through Carrier linkage. The BACnet points cover setpoints, space and supply temperatures, airflow, damper position, occupancy, terminal mode and alarms.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet ARC156"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The points list also prints lux_bn (lux sensor) with no BACnet object ID; it is left out here.",
  "Terminal Mode (terminal_status, MSV:2006) runs across a page break in the guide; its states are joined from both pages.",
  "System points (system_spt, system_rh, system_iaq, system_oat, system_stpt_adj) default to -999, meaning no network value.",
  "Air Source points (link_*) and Airside Linkage Status only carry data when the zone is linked to a Carrier air source.",
  "The airflow setpoints are not in the BACnet list; Flow Input (AI:1) reports measured airflow."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "VAV Zone II Controllers Installation and Start-up Guide (Appendix D: BACnet points list)",
  "doc_number": "11-808-602-01",
  "revision_date": "2026-02-19",
  "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1000/Public/0E/11-808-602-01.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Give the controller a unique MS/TP address on the rotary switches (the factory 00 must be changed) and match the network baud. For third-party occupancy control, disable Occupancy Schedules and write BAS On/Off (keypad_ovrde). Write occupied/unoccupied setpoints directly, and write system_spt if the space temperature comes from the network.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "MV 1001",
    "name": "keypad_ovrde",
    "why": "BAS occupancy command: 2 = occupied, 3 = unoccupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 9001",
    "name": "shutdown",
    "why": "Network shutdown command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3001",
    "name": "occ_cl_stpt",
    "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3002",
    "name": "occ_ht_stpt",
    "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 2006",
    "name": "terminal_status",
    "why": "Current zone mode (heating, cooling, vent...)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 2008",
    "name": "occ_status",
    "why": "Confirms occupied/unoccupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2007",
    "name": "space_temp",
    "why": "Space temperature the zone controls to"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1",
    "name": "flow_input",
    "why": "Measured airflow, CFM"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1013",
    "name": "dpr_pos",
    "why": "Damper position, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 7001",
    "name": "spt_fail",
    "why": "No valid space temperature; local heat/cool off"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BAS On/Off (keypad_ovrde, MSV:1001) gives a third-party BMS control of occupancy: 1 = Inactive, 2 = Occupied, 3 = Unoccupied. Occupancy Schedules must be set to Disable for it to work, and setting Occupied or Unoccupied turns Optimal Start off. Shutdown (BV:9001) stops the zone; VAV Reheat (BV:1029) and Heat Enable (BV:1012) enable reheat and heating.",
  "heartbeat": "No general heartbeat. A slave zone that was linked raises the Airside Linkage alarm (air_linkage_fail, BV:7030) if it gets no linkage data for 5 minutes.",
  "remote_sensors": "A network space temperature must be written to system_spt (AV:1902) every 1 to 5 minutes. Network RH, CO2, OAT and setpoint adjust go to system_rh, system_iaq, system_oat and system_stpt_adj; -999 means no network value. Without any valid space temperature the zone alarms and stops local heating and cooling.",
  "setup": [
   "MS/TP address is set on the Tens and Ones rotary switches; the factory 00 must be changed. The address is read at power-up.",
   "MS/TP runs at 9600, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8 kbps (DIP switches); ARC156 runs at 156 kbps via the ARC156/MS/TP jumper.",
   "A VAV Master can take up to 63 slave zones; linked controllers on one MS/TP network must be addressed in sequence."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Shutdown (BV:9001) is printed with a default of Active (1) in this guide; check its state before commissioning.",
   "Never connect an MS/TP or ARCNET network to the Act Net port; it is only for Carrier actuators and Smart Valves.",
   "Air Source points read nothing on a stand-alone zone (no linkage)."
  ]
 },
